		{
			description: [
				"When a Create machine stops, begin at the power source. Use goggles to verify rotation, follow every shaft and gearbox, then check the network's stress capacity and RPM."
				"A source can be spinning while the network is overstressed. Increasing speed may make the problem worse because many components consume more stress at higher RPM."
				"Test machines one operation at a time. A visible temporary shaft is better than a beautiful hidden network nobody can debug."
				"When a device is silent, trace rotation from the source one block at a time with Engineer's Goggles. Check reversed gearboxes, disconnected shafts, incorrect faces, overstress, and recipe requirements in that order."
			]
			id: "4EAA9A43A9020901"
			rewards: [{
				id: "36C6E00E1A980E65"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Trace power from source to work"
			tasks: [{
				id: "729D436B8DA20974"
				title: "I read and understood these field notes"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Diagnosing a Silent Machine"
			x: -1.5d
			y: 6.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["4EAA9A43A9020901"]
			description: [
				"Saws, drills, belts and moving contraptions interact with entities and loose items. Fence dangerous work areas, provide maintenance access and keep emergency shutoffs obvious."
				"Back up complicated designs with screenshots or written signs showing direction and purpose. The person repairing the machine tomorrow may not be the person building it today."
				"The field engineers say every elegant machine has two outputs: the product, and an explanation another player can understand."
				"Create's design language is motion you can read. The workshop guild values a slower machine that teaches its own operation more than a compact tangle that only its absent builder understands."
			]
			id: "10F60FD4BC979CDC"
			rewards: [{
				id: "3FD2DFAD5EE8D041"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Moving blocks deserve clear space"
			tasks: [{
