				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Workshop Safety"
			x: 1.5d
			y: 6.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Choose an unfamiliar Create component, hover it in JEI or inventory, and hold the Ponder key. Pause, rotate, and step through every scene until you can state input, output, motion, and required neighbouring blocks."
				"Rebuild the demonstration as a small exposed test rather than copying a screenshot into the final factory. Use Engineer's Goggles to verify rotation and read any stress or speed information."
				"Explain the component to another player without reopening Ponder, then compare your explanation with the scene. The lesson is complete when the animation has become working knowledge rather than a video you once watched."
			]
			id: "7387B28B144B5CEE"
			rewards: [{
				id: "6FA28176C1EA0594"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Read one machine before crafting it"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7476DFBBFFF5F288"
				title: "I read this field lesson and tried its method"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Workshop Course: The Ponder Exam"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7387B28B144B5CEE"]
			description: [
				"Build one rotational source, a visible shaft, a speed-changing stage, and several controllable loads. Read RPM, stress capacity, and stress impact with Goggles before and after each change."
				"Deliberately overstress the network, observe that it stops, then recover by reducing load, speed, or adding appropriate capacity. This controlled failure makes later factory diagnostics much faster."
				"Label the bench with the difference between speed and power, including one measured example from the installed machines. Leave it intact as a training tool so new engineers can experiment without interrupting the food line or railway."
			]
			id: "4F175E65CB686F00"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2442AE76639E0E2D"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Measure source, speed, load, and failure"
