			title: "Workshop Course: Build a Stress Test Bench"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["4F175E65CB686F00"]
			description: [
				"Choose one raw material and inspect every Create recipe category it participates in. Build small stations for two different processes and compare inputs, outputs, by-products, heat, and stress."
				"Fans require an air stream through the correct medium; presses need the correct surface; mixers need basins and sometimes heated Blaze Burners; deployers and slicers need correct orientation and held items."
				"Feed one item manually, then one stack, then automate only after the result is stable. A process matrix beside the workshop prevents recipes from becoming unexplained machines copied from the internet."
			]
			id: "775E6DB58C79670F"
			rewards: [{
				id: "57F49E65DFFBD9A6"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Mill, press, fan, mix, and cut"
